<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Conference of Ambassadors</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1920">1920</a>–<a href="/years/1931">1931</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Conference of Ambassadors was a body of the Allied powers set up in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> in 1920 to enforce and interpret the peace treaties after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. Made up of the ambassadors of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> under a French chair, it settled frontier questions: in November 1921 it confirmed Albania's 1913 borders, ending Yugoslav backing for the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mirdita">Mirdita</a>, and in 1923 it fixed the Polish–Lithuanian border.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/conference-of-ambassadors.jpg" alt="Conference of Ambassadors" width="320" height="148" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roke, Hoshie · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Council-of-Ambassadors-map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
